
# SimpleEmployeeAPI

A simple in-memory CRUD REST API built with ASP.NET Core — my first .NET Web API practice exercise.

## What It Does

Manages a list of employees entirely in memory (no database). Supports full Create, Read, Update, and Delete operations via HTTP endpoints, testable through a browser or Postman.

## Tech Stack

- ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET)
- C#
- In-memory List (no database)

## Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/employees` | Retrieve all employees |
| GET | `/api/employees/{id}` | Retrieve a single employee by ID |
| POST | `/api/employees` | Create a new employee |
| PUT | `/api/employees/{id}` | Update an existing employee |
| DELETE | `/api/employees/{id}` | Delete an employee |

## How to Run

**Prerequisites:** .NET SDK installed

```bash
# Clone the repo and navigate to this folder
cd SimpleEmployeeAPI

# Run the API
dotnet run
```

Then open your browser or Postman and hit:
```
https://localhost:5001/api/employees
```

## Example POST Body

```json
{
  "name": "John",
  "position": "Manager"
}
```

